{{!-- One "labelled list of PAIRED rows" on the Create-a-Site wizard: a first field carrying the
      delete button, and a second indented under it.

      The sibling of cs-line-list.hbs and here for the same reason. Questions & answers and
      Denizens collect exactly this shape and differed only in their wording and in whether
      suggestion chips sit above the rows, yet the block was pasted twice. The JS side was already
      fully generic — `_PAIR_LISTS` names each list's keys, `blankRow` and `_pairRows` read that
      table, and one delegated `.stonetop-cs-add` handler keys on `data-list` — so only the markup
      stood between the wizard and a third paired list.

      NOT the timeline, which is genuinely a different shape (both fields on one row, no indent).

      Row values are reached with `lookup` rather than named directly, which is what lets one
      block serve lists whose keys differ; `_PAIR_LISTS` is where those key names are declared.

      Context: the dialog's own, plus
        list          the `data-list` key every handler here reads ("denizens")
        label         the heading
        hint          optional parenthetical beside the heading, WITHOUT its brackets
        chips         optional click-to-fill suggestions ({text, used}), filling keyA
        rows          this list's rows ({index, ...keys})
        keyA / keyB   the two field names, in the order they render
        placeholderA  the first field's placeholder
        placeholderB  the second field's placeholder
        addLabel      the add button's wording ("Add denizen") --}}
<div class="stonetop-cf-gear">
  <div class="stonetop-cf-pick-label">{{label}}{{#if hint}} <span class="stonetop-cf-pick-hint">({{hint}})</span>{{/if}}</div>
  {{#if chips}}
  <div class="stonetop-cf-chips">
    {{#each chips}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-cf-chip stonetop-cs-suggest{{#if used}} is-selected{{/if}}" data-list="{{../list}}" data-text="{{text}}">{{text}}</button>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}
  {{#each rows}}
  <div class="stonetop-cs-pair-row">
    <div class="stonetop-cf-gear-row">
      <input type="text" class="stonetop-cf-input stonetop-cs-pair" data-list="{{../list}}" data-index="{{index}}" data-key="{{../keyA}}" value="{{lookup this ../keyA}}" placeholder="{{../placeholderA}}">
      <button type="button" class="stonetop-cs-remove stonetop-cf-mini-btn stonetop-cf-mini-btn--danger" data-list="{{../list}}" data-index="{{index}}"><i class="fas fa-times"></i></button>
    </div>
    <input type="text" class="stonetop-cf-input stonetop-cs-pair stonetop-cs-answer" data-list="{{../list}}" data-index="{{index}}" data-key="{{../keyB}}" value="{{lookup this ../keyB}}" placeholder="{{../placeholderB}}">
  </div>
  {{/each}}
  <button type="button" class="stonetop-cs-add stonetop-cf-mini-btn" data-list="{{list}}"><i class="fas fa-plus"></i> {{addLabel}}</button>
</div>
